Subject: dxgi: prefer GL present for top-level non-popup swapchain windows

Live's GPU renderer creates a D3D11 swapchain covering its whole main
window. wined3d's swapchain_present sends SEQUENTIAL and FLIP_SEQUENTIAL
swapchains to swapchain_blit_gdi unless WINED3D_SWAPCHAIN_PREFER_GL_PRESENT
is set, and that path is a full-window GPU readback plus a full-window
XPutImage upload - the code puts it at ~5-10ms per frame.

Measured on a 2560x1350 window under a scripted mouse-move sweep, with the
only difference between builds being this patch:

  without: 645.6 / 671.2 MB/s,  119.9% / 95.3% of a core
  with   :   0.41 /   0.40 MB/s,  21.8% / 20.2% of a core

The path change is directly observable rather than inferred: the fire-once
FIXME("Using GDI present.") in swapchain_blit_gdi fires once on a full Live
startup without this patch and not at all with it, so the readback function
stops being called rather than merely getting cheaper.

(The exact swap effect in play is not FLIP_SEQUENTIAL or FLIP_DISCARD -
wined3d's "Unimplemented swap effect" FIXME never fires - but SEQUENTIAL
has not been distinguished from DISCARD-plus-partial-copy, as five separate
conditions reach the same branch. The measurement above does not depend on
which one it is.)

PREFER_GL_PRESENT already exists and is documented as avoiding exactly this
readback, but it was only ever set in dxgi/factory.c for DComp composition
targets that are top-level. A plain top-level swapchain window - Live's main
window - never went through that branch and so never got the flag.

Set it at swapchain creation for top-level device windows, excluding both
WS_CHILD and WS_POPUP. Two earlier revisions got this wrong. The first tested only the parent and
flagged every top-level window. The second also excluded WS_POPUP, which was
still not enough: CreateSwapChainForComposition creates its own
"WineDCompSwapchain" window with WS_CHILD parented to the desktop, so
GetAncestor(GA_PARENT) returns the desktop and a parent-only test classifies
it as top-level. That flagged every DComp composition swapchain, and the
windows they back - Live's Settings and authorisation dialogs - painted black
until interacted with, intermittently, because the swap goes to a child
window with no on-screen drawable. The GDI blit is immune because it
writes through the window surface, which survives map/expose. Note that
WS_POPUP and WS_CAPTION coexist - Live's Settings window is framed and still
WS_POPUP (style 96c80000) - so a title bar is not evidence of a non-popup.

Child and embedded plugin windows have no whole_window and keep the GDI blit
as before. The DComp target path runs later and re-decides per target, so its
choice still wins where it applies, and swapchain_present independently falls
back to the GDI blit if the GL context did not bind (dc == backup_dc), so a
failed bind is not fatal.

See notes/FINDINGS-GPU-RENDERER-PRESENT-STORM-2026-07-28.md.

diff --git a/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c b/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
index b4ed824..ce226b0 100644
--- a/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
+++ b/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
@@ -1187,6 +1187,51 @@ HRESULT d3d11_swapchain_init(struct d3d11_swapchain *swapchain, struct dxgi_devi
         goto cleanup;
     }
 
+    /* A top-level window has an X11 whole_window, so wined3d can present it
+     * with glXSwapBuffers instead of the GDI fallback.  Without this a
+     * SEQUENTIAL/FLIP_SEQUENTIAL swapchain takes swapchain_blit_gdi on every
+     * present: a full-window GPU readback plus a full-window XPutImage upload
+     * (~5-10ms/frame, and ~600MB/s of X11 traffic for a 2560x1350 window under
+     * sustained repaints - see
+     * notes/FINDINGS-GPU-RENDERER-PRESENT-STORM-2026-07-28.md).  Live's main
+     * window is top-level and hits exactly that path once its GPU renderer is
+     * enabled.  Child/embedded windows have no whole_window and must keep the
+     * GDI blit, so they are left alone; the DComp target path in
+     * dxgi/factory.c re-decides this per target and runs after this.
+     *
+     * Both WS_CHILD and WS_POPUP are excluded, and the WS_CHILD half is the
+     * one that matters most: dxgi_factory_CreateSwapChainForComposition
+     * creates its own "WineDCompSwapchain" window with WS_CHILD and the
+     * desktop as parent, so GetAncestor(GA_PARENT) returns the desktop and a
+     * parent-only test wrongly classifies it as top-level.  That flagged
+     * every DComp composition swapchain for GL present and left the windows
+     * they back (Live's Settings and authorisation dialogs) painting black
+     * until interacted with, intermittently - the swap goes to a child
+     * window that has no on-screen drawable, while the GDI blit writes
+     * through the window surface and is unaffected.
+     *
+     * WS_POPUP is excluded for the same reason on the popup's own swapchain.
+     * Note WS_POPUP and WS_CAPTION coexist - Live's Settings window is framed
+     * and still WS_POPUP (style 96c80000) - so a title bar is not evidence
+     * that a window is not a popup. */
+    if (desc->device_window)
+    {
+        HWND parent = GetAncestor(desc->device_window, GA_PARENT);
+        LONG style = GetWindowLongW(desc->device_window, GWL_STYLE);
+
+        if ((!parent || parent == GetDesktopWindow()) && !(style & (WS_CHILD | WS_POPUP)))
+        {
+            static unsigned int flagged;
+            WCHAR cls[64] = {0};
+
+            GetClassNameW(desc->device_window, cls, ARRAY_SIZE(cls));
+            if (++flagged <= 8)
+                TRACE("GL present for device window %p class %s style %08lx.\n",
+                        desc->device_window, debugstr_w(cls), style);
+            wined3d_swapchain_set_prefer_gl_present(swapchain->wined3d_swapchain, TRUE);
+        }
+    }
+
     state = wined3d_swapchain_get_state(swapchain->wined3d_swapchain);
     wined3d_swapchain_state_get_size(state, &desc->backbuffer_width, &desc->backbuffer_height);
 
